WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:04.970
- [Narrator] China's army of
snow guns is paving the way

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.853
for a smooth Winter Olympics.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:12.630
It's the first games to
rely entirely on fake snow

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:15.750
and Beijing isn't the first
host city to make fresh powder.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:17.040
Others have done it too,

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.270
supplementing real snow on mountain tracks

00:00:19.270 --> 00:00:21.543
for the world's best
skiers and snowboarders.

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.980
- For producing artificial snow,

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:27.740
they require huge amounts of water.

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:31.470
It's nearly 2 million
cubic meters of water.

00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:33.130
- [Narrator] That would be enough to fill

00:00:34.935 --> 00:00:35.768
about 800 Olympic size swimming pools

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:38.150
and trying to access that
amount in a water scare city

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:39.430
isn't the only feat.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:42.144
Snowmakers also have
to battle the elements.

00:00:42.144 --> 00:00:46.540
- (speaking in foreign language)

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.130
- [Narrator] This isn't
just a challenge for China

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:49.883
because as the world gets warmer,

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:53.290
other host cities may not be cold enough

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:56.290
and end up using more artificial snow too.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:59.000
We take a look at the logistics
and environmental impact

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.150
behind China's snow making process

00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:03.379
to see what means for the future

00:01:03.379 --> 00:01:04.913
of the world's biggest sporting event.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:09.270
The first hurdle China needs to clear,

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.573
make sure there's enough
water to make snow.

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:14.705
The games are divided into
three zones that are in an area

00:01:14.705 --> 00:01:17.140
with low precipitation during winter

00:01:18.176 --> 00:01:20.040
and not ideal for creating
alpine conditions.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:22.760
- Because it's one of the
driest region of China

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:25.980
that's already suffering
from severe water stress.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.500
- [Narrator] Carmen De
Jong is a geographer

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:30.860
who's been studying artificial
snow's environmental impact

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:32.706
not just at the Olympics

00:01:32.706 --> 00:01:34.830
but also ski resorts and
indoor sporting venues.

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:37.590
- So there's not enough
water available locally.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.980
It has to be transported
from very far away.

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:41.068
- [Narrator] De Jong says one
of the zones sources water

00:01:41.068 --> 00:01:44.430
from reservoir 18 miles away

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.870
and supplies nearby farms and residents.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:49.380
And some parts of that
route are on an incline.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.910
- They've had to build pumping stations

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:53.090
to pump the water uphill

00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:55.450
to reach all the snow
guns and snow cannons.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:02:00.085
So all the Olympic ski runs have pipelines

00:02:00.085 --> 00:02:04.180
running underground to supply with water

00:02:04.180 --> 00:02:08.160
and electricity in order
to manufacture the snow.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:10.070
- [Narrator] This is an
energy-intensive process,

00:02:10.070 --> 00:02:12.423
according to sport
ecologist, Madeline Orr,

00:02:13.477 --> 00:02:14.940
who wrote a report about
the impact of climate change

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:16.690
on the Winter Olympics.

00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:19.670
Take, for example, covering
one track from top to bottom.

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:22.907
- The amount of snow guns that
would be needed to produce

00:02:22.907 --> 00:02:24.810
the snow for that for a
day is roughly equivalent

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.940
to a small apartment building.

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.870
- [Narrator] This entire process
requires closed supervision

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:32.673
and China has created
its own snow making team.

00:02:33.531 --> 00:02:37.614
- (speaking in foreign language)

00:02:43.051 --> 00:02:43.920
- [Narrator] Since 2017,

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.300
these scientists have been
developing artificial snow

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.070
that would be suitable for the region.

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:49.880
- [Carmen] The soil is so dry

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:53.271
that the artificial snow
doesn't stick to the ground.

00:02:53.271 --> 00:02:57.080
There's also the problem
of a lot of evaporation.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:00.222
- [Narrator] De Jong says
a way around this issue

00:03:00.222 --> 00:03:01.055
is injecting water into the soil,

00:03:01.055 --> 00:03:04.893
creating a frozen layer optimal
for fake snow to then stick.

00:03:05.793 --> 00:03:07.790
- (speaking in foreign language).

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:09.970
- [Narrator] The region is
also prone to strong winds,

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:13.379
which doesn't help when it
comes time to spray the area.

00:03:13.379 --> 00:03:17.462
- (speaking in foreign language)

00:03:23.240 --> 00:03:25.370
- [Narrator] As much as
Beijing or any future host city

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.080
may want to control the weather,

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:29.210
sport ecologist, Madeline Orr says,

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:31.860
there's no amount of artificial
snow that can make up

00:03:32.805 --> 00:03:33.638
for the lack of cold.

00:03:33.638 --> 00:03:35.860
- The problem is there is
no perfect sustainability

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:37.830
when you're producing a winter event

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:39.200
in a summer destination.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:42.140
And so, no matter what you do
to be more energy efficient,

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:44.823
the design of the event is unsustainable.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:48.800
- [Narrator] The Beijing
Organizing Committee

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.190
says artificial snow
making has minimal impact

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:52.820
on the local water supply,

00:03:52.820 --> 00:03:55.650
because it uses a water
conservation system.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:57.140
The International Olympic Committee

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.076
said it's treating climate
change as a serious challenge

00:03:59.076 --> 00:04:03.320
and that artificial snow
production should be sustainable.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.750
It said host regions must have

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:06.110
sufficiently cold temperatures

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:08.890
and will be required
to be climate positive.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:11.270
Orr says the best option
may be to not choose

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.100
a future location like Beijing.

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.600
- It's okay to supplement
with artificial snow.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:17.970
Some athletes like that it's extra speedy,

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:20.650
but it can't be a hundred percent again.

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:23.150
(light music)

